{
  "$comment": [
    "Published engine artifacts, and the hashes that make them safe to reuse.",
    "",
    "Read by ports/lib/fetch-engine.mjs, which downloads each file, checks its size and sha256",
    "against this table, and only then puts it in place. Every sha256 here was computed from the",
    "bytes actually built and tested on this machine (see docs/fetch-engine-artifacts.md for how),",
    "against the upstream commit recorded in `upstream`. If a file is rebuilt, its hash changes and",
    "this entry must be regenerated by the publish workflow rather than edited by hand.",
    "",
    "`repository` + `releaseTag` give the download URL: <repository>/releases/download/<releaseTag>/<name>.",
    "The tag convention is engine-<engine>-<version>. Until the publish workflow creates a release,",
    "a fetch on a machine that does not already have the file reports it as unavailable (exit 2) and",
    "the caller falls back to building from source, which is the intended behaviour."
  ],
